text:
rebecca: Heads-up — noticed a bunch of tenants with "preview" invoices showing more tokens than ledger tonight. numbers look like "ghost" tokens attaching to a new shard after transport fallback.

omar: Ghost tokens? sample please.

rebecca: Sanitized trace: 
```
{"fingerprint":"fp-7a","tenant":"t-zen","session_cookie":"sc-13","route_shard":"shard-A","tokens":64}
...later...
{"fingerprint":"fp-7a","tenant":"t-zen","session_cookie":"sc-99","route_shard":"shard-B","tokens":62}
```
Ledger uses fingerprint dedupe so final billed tokens ~64. Preview groups by session_cookie|route_shard so it sums to ~126.

priya: Ah — route-decider issues a refreshed sticky cookie on fallback. preview agg keying picks up cookie changes and treats them as separate origins.

lee: Two options: 1) upstream: make the sticky cookie stable for the lifetime of the session (or return a billing_shard_id that is stable regardless of transport), or 2) downstream: change preview pipeline to reconcile by fingerprint when multiple cookies seen for same fingerprint within the same join window.

omar: Upstream sounds clean but risky: touching route-decider, proxies, mobile SDKs. How many consumers rely on cookie semantics today?

priya: Several features use cookie mutability (A/B routing, regional affinity). Hard to freeze without coordination. Upstream plan would need a compat window and clear docs. estimate 3-5 days with QA and migration.

lee: Downstream mitigation is faster. Proposal: preview-agg should check for events sharing fingerprint inside the same 30s window and collapse them into a single billing tuple, emitting the fingerprint as a transient grouping key. No partitioning changes.

rebecca: That seems reasonable for a stop-gap. But preview is latency-sensitive — can the reconciliation step be fast?

omar: Implementation sketch: during window reduce, build two maps: by_cookie_key and by_fingerprint. If a fingerprint maps to multiple cookie keys, emit a single fingerprint-grouped sum and add a tag so dashboards show reconciled rows. Pseudocode: 
```js
// reduce for window
const byCookie = new Map()
const byFp = new Map()
for (e of events) {
  const ck = `${e.tenant}|${e.session_cookie}|${e.route_shard}`
  byCookie[ck] = (byCookie[ck]||0)+e.tokens
  if (e.fingerprint) byFp[e.fingerprint] = (byFp[e.fingerprint]||0)+e.tokens
}
// emit fingerprint groups where collisions seen
for (fp in byFp) {
  if (fp maps to >1 cookie) emit(`fp:${fp}`, byFp[fp], {reconciled:true})
}
// emit remaining cookie-only groups as before
```

priya: We should also surface reconciliation telemetry: percent of preview tokens reconciled by fingerprint, and a per-tenant heatmap of cookie churn. alert if reconciliation rate > 8% for top tenants.

rebecca: Agreed. Also add a small opt-in debug header x-billing-trace for a tenant so we can trace a session through route-decider -> proxies -> ingest -> preview without sampling all traffic.

ops-bot: Created ticket MET-9905: "preview shard ghosting from cookie refresh" and attached sample traces.

omar: Roll plan for downstream fix: feature flag preview.reconcile_by_fp off default. Canary 3% tenants for 15m, check preview-vs-ledger delta, CPU and tail latency. If stable, ramp 20%->100% over 3h. Rollback: flip flag.

lee: I'll own the preview-agg patch. priya will draft the upstream RFC for a stable billing_shard_id (long-term). rebecca will add dashboards and alerts.

priya: RFC note: if we do billing_shard_id, make it optional in the proto (billing_shard_id), consumers fallback to fingerprint/request_id when absent. plan dual-write of kafka key for 48h when changing partitioning.

rebecca: Action items summarized: lee -> implement canary reconciliation patch (MET-9905), priya -> draft billing_shard_id RFC + migration plan, rebecca -> dashboard + debug header runbook. target: mitigation canary today, RFC in 48h.

om ar: Will post PR link and perf numbers here once canary runs. ping me immediately if preview delta > 12% for any tenant.

rebecca: Thanks team — mitigation + telemetry should keep customers calm while we decide on upstream changes. :thumbsup:
